WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
If your prep is MiraLAX, this video will walk you through exactly how to take

2
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:03.920
it.

3
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.080
Just follow along step by step.

4
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.610
For this prep, you'll need a few items, all available over the counter, no

5
00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:11.200
prescription needed.

6
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.650
You'll need one 238 gram bottle of MiraLAX powder, two to four Dulcolax laxative

7
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:17.600
tablets

8
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:23.040
and 64 ounces of a clear sports drink like Gatorade, Propel or Crystal Light.

9
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.560
That's usually 232 ounce bottles.

10
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.280
If you have diabetes, use sugar-free Gatorade G2.

11
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.000
Also, make sure you get the laxative tablets, not the stool softener.

12
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.680
One important rule, your sports drink cannot be red, orange, blue or purple.

13
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.400
Stick to clear or light colored flavors.

14
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:47.360
The day before your colonoscopy, you'll start by mixing the solution.

15
00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:52.210
Pour the entire bottle of MiraLAX into a pitcher with all 64 ounces of the

16
00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:53.120
sports drink.

17
00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:56.320
Stir or shake until the powder is completely dissolved.

18
00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.750
You can chill it in the refrigerator if you'd like, keeping it cold makes it

19
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:00.720
easier to drink.

20
00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:04.560
Now for part one, the evening before your procedure.

21
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:10.080
At 5 p.m., take your Dulcolax tablets with a glass of water.

22
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:13.680
Your doctor's instructions will tell you whether to take two or four.

23
00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.920
Follow their guidance on the specific amount.

24
00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.560
At 6 p.m., you'll start drinking the first half of the solution.

25
00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.240
That's 32 ounces.

26
00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.840
Drink an eight ounce glass every 15 minutes until that half is gone.

27
00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.560
Keep drinking clear liquids after you finish.

28
00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.560
For part two, six hours before your colonoscopy, you'll drink the second half,

29
00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.240
which is another 32 ounces.

30
00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.720
Drink this at the same pace, an eight ounce glass every 15 minutes.

31
00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:44.500
You can continue to have clear liquids up until four hours before your

32
00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:45.360
procedure.

33
00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.600
This part is really important.

34
00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:52.130
You must drink all of the prep solution as directed, even if you're already

35
00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:52.640
passing clear

36
00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:56.790
liquid. I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what

37
00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:57.200
gives us

38
00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.360
the clearest view during your procedure.

39
00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.680
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule, and neither

40
00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:04.400
of us wants that.

41
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:08.720
Please drink plenty of liquids throughout the process to prevent dehydration.

42
00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:12.880
Staying hydrated will help you feel better and help the prep do its job.

43
00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:17.280
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom,

44
00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.800
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

45
00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:27.000
That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay

46
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:27.600
hydrated.

47
00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:32.230
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office. We're here

48
00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:33.280
to help.
